<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- The press on the From half: not a box laid on the half, the half.

     It used to be a rectangle rounded on all four corners with a 1dp ring of
     its own, laid over the paper. At the seam that left two rounded corners
     curling away from the split, and the ring drew a second hairline a half
     pixel inside the card's own — the feedback read as a smaller box sitting on
     the box you pressed, slightly off-centre, and the beige under it was too
     faint to carry the state on its own.

     So the shape is the half itself: the card's 16dp on the three sides that
     are the card's edge, square on the side that is the seam, so the fill runs
     into the split and is cut by the seam line rather than floating beside it.
     No stroke: the card already has one, and a press does not need a second. -->
<shape xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:shape="rectangle">
    <solid android:color="@color/screen_half_press" />
    <corners
        android:bottomLeftRadius="16dp"
        android:bottomRightRadius="0dp"
        android:topLeftRadius="16dp"
        android:topRightRadius="0dp" />
</shape>
